            "content": [
              {
                "type": "output_text",
                "text": "I don’t have live web access, so I can’t verify the absolute latest Mars Perseverance rover news in real time. As of my latest reliable knowledge, Perseverance was still operating in Jezero Crater, studying ancient river-delta and lakebed rocks for evidence of past habitability and collecting rock-core samples for possible future return to Earth.\n\nKey recent developments up to that point included:\n\n- **Ongoing sample collection:** Perseverance has cached multiple scientifically valuable Martian rock and regolith samples.\n- **Exploration of Jezero Crater’s ancient delta:** The rover has been examining sedimentary rocks that may preserve signs of ancient microbial life, if it ever existed.\n- **Ingenuity helicopter mission ended:** NASA’s Ingenuity Mars Helicopter, which arrived with Perseverance, completed its mission after far exceeding expectations with dozens of flights. Its operations ended after rotor damage was detected.\n- **Mars Sample Return under review:** NASA and partners have been reassessing the cost, schedule, and architecture of the planned mission to bring Perseverance’s samples back to Earth.\n\nFor the most current updates, the best sources are NASA’s Perseverance mission page, NASA/JPL news releases, and the rover’s official social media channels.",
